spla
------------------------------------------
SPLA provides specialized functions for linear algebra computations with a C++
and C interface, which are inspired by requirements in computational material
science codes.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  liblapack0-3.12.0-1
  libopenmpi40-4.1.6-1
  libspla-devel-1.6.1-1bl1
  libspla1-1.6.1-1bl1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cli11-2.7.2-1bl1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-fortran-14.4.0-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libevent-devel-2.1.13-1
  libgtest-devel-1.18.0-1bl1
  libhwloc-devel-2.13.0-1
  liblapack-devel-3.12.0-1
  libopenmpi-devel-4.1.6-1
  libscalapack-devel-2.2.3-1bl1
  ninja-1.13.2-1
  zlib-devel-1.3.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/eth-cscs/spla

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/eth-cscs/spla/archive/refs/tags/v1.6.1.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack spla-1.6.1-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./spla-1.6.1-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/spla-1.6.1-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/spla-1.6.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libspla1-1.6.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libspla-devel-1.6.1-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

